                <pb facs="0744" n="632" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg632"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/4591: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Poole</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Archangel</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-27T15:00:00+03:31"><hi rendition="#italic">May 27, 1919, 3
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 27, 8:28
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1237 [<hi rendition="#italic">1227</hi>]. 122 [<hi rendition="#italic">123</hi>]
                    to Paris. The first contingent of the British expedition, numbering slightly
                    more than 4,000, arrived yesterday. They were formally welcomed today by the
                    local government and passed in review under a triumphal arch.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Poole</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
